The SSR story's cue groups
==========================

What the storyboard (`storyboard.lam`) says again and again, said once: the package `godot_ssr_story`, which
the storyboard imports (`$$[Import* godot_ssr_story]`; tools/video/build.py gives it to the reader).

$[Import* std]$[Import* content]$[Import* present]$[Import* render_lab]$[Import* godot_ssr]

A beat's opening keys: its demonstration and panel, the callout and the insets cleared; `more` are the beat's own.

$[# {opening demo panel more} {append {' demo {callout ""} {inset ""} panel} more}]

The room as the story shows it: a polished metal floor, no sky in the reflections, SSR on, every stage drawn, and no height field or cross-section over it.

$[# baseRoom {append {append {' {floorMetallic 1.0} {skyReflection 0.0} {ssrEnabled 1.0} {ssrComposeStep 3.0} {floorRoughness 0.15} {pickX -1.0} {pickY -1.0}} {view "field" {' {fieldShow 0.0} {fieldMorph 0.0} {fieldLevel 0.0} {fieldZoom 0.0} {fieldTurn 0.0} {fieldTilt 50.0}}}} {view "profile" {' {profileShow 0.0}}}}]

A camera low over the floor, the teapot and the sphere reflected in it.

$[# lowCamera {' {cameraTarget {' 0.0 0.55 -0.6}} {cameraYaw 18.0} {cameraPitch 10.0} {cameraDistance 5.6}}]

The march's worked example: P on the inside of the teapot's spout, whose ray crosses the gap to the teapot's body (far
wall's low columns, then the body's tall ones). A camera close beside the teapot, the spout clear of the trace's inset.

$[# spoutCamera {' {cameraTarget {' -0.15 0.38 -1.7}} {cameraYaw 35.0} {cameraPitch 12.0} {cameraDistance 1.8}}]

P is an SSR pixel, and the panel beside the scene sets the scene's width, so the same spot of the spout is a pixel of
its own for each panel: beside the values panel (613 by 364 SSR pixels) and beside the trace listing's code panel (522
by 364: a recording fits the code panel to its listing, ui::code_panel_fit, so a change to that listing moves it). The
two pyramids' cells fall differently, so the two walks differ after the first iterations; the story narrates the code
panel's.

$[# spoutValues {' {pickX 368.0} {pickY 198.0}}]
$[# spoutCode {' {pickX 297.0} {pickY 198.0}}]
